WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.109
Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification, commonly called CMMC 2.

2
00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:14.248
0, is the Department of Defense program for verifying that defense contractors implement required safeguards for sensitive unclassified information.

3
00:00:14.248 --> 00:00:29.474
The program applies within the Defense Industrial Base, or DIB: the large ecosystem of prime contractors, subcontractors, suppliers, service providers, and other organizations that support Department of Defense missions and contracts.

4
00:00:29.474 --> 00:00:38.504
CMMC focuses on Federal Contract Information, known as FCI, and Controlled Unclassified Information, known as CUI.

5
00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:47.034
The information an organization receives, creates, stores, processes, or transmits helps determine which requirements may apply.

6
00:00:47.034 --> 00:00:54.188
The program uses three levels that correspond to increasing information sensitivity and cybersecurity expectations.

7
00:00:54.188 --> 00:01:00.834
It also uses assessment and affirmation mechanisms to provide confidence that required practices are implemented.

8
00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:07.988
CMMC does not replace every other contract clause, security obligation, or risk-management activity.

9
00:01:07.988 --> 00:01:18.155
Organizations remain responsible for reading the applicable solicitation and contract, understanding information flows, and satisfying all relevant requirements.

10
00:01:18.155 --> 00:01:22.316
A CMMC status is not simply a security product or document.

11
00:01:22.316 --> 00:01:32.912
It depends on people, processes, technology, governance, defined scope, evidence, and sustained operation across the environment that handles protected information.

12
00:01:32.912 --> 00:01:35.586
CMMC affects more than compliance staff.

13
00:01:35.586 --> 00:01:47.739
Executives, contract teams, engineers, administrators, developers, employees, and suppliers all influence whether information is handled within approved systems and protected as required.

14
00:01:47.739 --> 00:01:51.540
This course provides educational information about CMMC 2.

15
00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.957
0 concepts.

16
00:01:52.957 --> 00:02:00.291
It is not legal advice, compliance consulting, audit guidance, assessment preparation, or certification advice.

17
00:02:00.291 --> 00:02:05.899
Contract-specific questions require current official sources and qualified counsel or advisors.
